Analyze this {language} code for security vulnerabilities.

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- SQL injection (string concatenation or formatting in queries)
- XSS (unsanitized output to HTML/DOM)
- IDOR (direct object references without authorization checks)
- Missing authentication/authorization on sensitive operations
- Hardcoded secrets, API keys, passwords, tokens
- Path traversal (user-controlled file paths)
- Command injection (user input in shell/exec calls)
- Prompt injection (user data interpolated into LLM prompts without sanitization)

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "vulnerability_type": "SQL_INJECTION|XSS|IDOR|MISSING_AUTH|HARDCODED_SECRET|PATH_TRAVERSAL|COMMAND_INJECTION|PROMPT_INJECTION|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific vulnerability",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no vulnerabilities found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
